=== REASONING ===

Why this slice MUST block now (in priority order):

1. Honesty Covenant rule #7 — "No predecessor bypass — verify
   every predecessor (0001-0064) STATUS=DONE first". 24 logs are
   missing (0038..0061). Per rule #1 ("No red-as-green") and rule
   #3 ("No skip-and-assume"), running the §2..§6 verification
   commands against an incomplete predecessor set would either
   fabricate a green result against a partial table or fail and
   require BLOCKED anyway. The honest action is to BLOCK at §1.

2. Prompt's Blocked Path explicit text — "Predecessor not DONE —
   if any predecessor 0001-0064 log is missing or has STATUS !=
   DONE, W1 MUST block with the missing slice ID listed. Do NOT
   pick a subset of features and wire only those." The 24 IDs
   above are the literal slice IDs the rule asks for.

3. Prior final-gate precedent — phase-50-9999-final-gate.log at
   commit fe4fcf98a already blocked for the SAME reason (44/64
   missing then; 24/64 missing now after additional slice
   commits). W1's contract sits one level below the final gate;
   it cannot be DONE while the final gate is BLOCKED on the same
   set of missing predecessors.

4. SPAWiringSelfCheck would either fail or false-pass —
   - If we author the table to enumerate ONLY the 30 user-facing
     features currently in the registry, the self-check passes
     trivially today and STAYS green when the missing 24 land
     LATER without their components — a silent-drift trap.
   - If we author the table to enumerate the 14 missing IDs as
     well, the self-check fails immediately because the registry
     has no entries to bind to and the component files don't
     exist on disk.
   Either path produces a misleading W1 STATUS. Per Covenant
   rule #4 ("No field resurrection — don't add back deleted
   fields to 'fix' things") and the prompt's Blocked Path bullet
   "If the corresponding web/src/components/ai/AI*.tsx file does
   not exist, the predecessor slice that owns that feature is
   incomplete — block on that slice, do NOT scaffold the
   component here", the correct answer is to BLOCK.

5. The methodology + aivet rules are IDEMPOTENT and HIGH-LEVERAGE
   on a complete registry, but LOW-LEVERAGE on a partial one —
   adding W1-A and W1-B today would only enforce against the 30
   present components and would silently miss the 24 that land
   LATER. Better to land all five W1 deliverables (P11/P12,
   spa_wiring.go, spaWiring.ts, aivet rules, self-check tests)
   in a single commit AFTER the missing predecessors.

ADR-015 invariant impact of this BLOCKED run:
  - I3 (baseline intact): no diff = no risk. Every baseline
    surface (POST /chatbot heuristic, manual AlertStudio form,
    manual TripPlanner, etc.) is unchanged by this slice.
  - I5 (off-mode absence): no diff = no risk. The 30 wired AI
    surfaces continue to obey withAiFeature gating; the 24
    missing surfaces simply do not exist (which is also "absent
    in off mode" — vacuously satisfied, but not proven for the
    on-mode positive control).
  - I6 (404 in off mode): no diff = no risk for the 30 routes
    that exist; the 24 routes that don't exist are not 404 — they
    are 404 because they were never registered at all, which
    happens to satisfy the off-mode contract by accident.
  - I7 (no SQL bypass): no diff. The propose-only contract for
    the 14 RenderProposal + 1 RenderSuggestion features the
    0065 prompt enumerates is preserved — every "Apply to form"
    button still routes through the baseline form's existing
    Save handler.
  - I8 (no duplicate writers): no diff. No new write paths.

Methodology principles this slice WOULD codify (and which
remain uncodified for now):
  - P11 (Wired-or-absent): every guarded AI surface that ships
    a backend route MUST have its frontend counterpart call that
    route end-to-end when the feature is enabled.
  - P12 (No placeholder buttons): shipped AI components MUST
    NOT render an unconditionally `disabled` primary action with
    placeholder copy.

Both principles are observed in tree today by the 30 wired
components — they just are not yet WRITTEN INTO the methodology
and not yet ENFORCED by aivet.

